sec.p:
Prior research has demonstrated that incorporating evolutionary information from proteins enhances the performance of protein sequence analysis tasks, particularly in the context of proteins exhibiting low sequence similarity [36–38]. BLOSUM62 is a fundamental and widely utilized tool in bioinformatics. This substitution matrix plays a pivotal role in quantifying the similarity between amino acid sequences, facilitating the comparison of proteins and the identification of conserved regions across diverse biological entities. The scores within the BLOSUM62 matrix signify the probability of amino acid substitution by another amino. When considering the representation of a peptide (or protein) sequence \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
